      "id": "E13",
      "chapter": 13,
      "slug": "13-rare-events",
      "section": "13.14",
      "title": "A forbidden site is not a small probability",
      "lang": "en",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch2\" id=\"visual-E13\" data-batch2=\"E13\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E13</span><h3>A forbidden site is not a small probability</h3></header><p class=\"\">After n steps of ±1, only sites of the same parity as n are possible. A Gaussian density needs the actual cell width to approximate an atom.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-lattice-n=\"4\" aria-pressed=\"true\">n=4</button><button type=\"button\" data-lattice-n=\"5\" aria-pressed=\"false\">n=5</button><button type=\"button\" data-lattice-n=\"6\" aria-pressed=\"false\">n=6</button></div><div class=\"b2-pair\"><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>Exact discrete masses</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E13-en-4.svg\" alt=\"Parity lattice with exact binomial masses\" data-lattice-scene></section><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>Density × standardized width</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E13-en-4-w2.svg\" alt=\"Local-density rectangle with the selected lattice width\" data-cell-scene></section></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-cell-width=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Actual width 2</button><button type=\"button\" data-cell-width=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Incorrect width 1</button></div><figcaption id=\"visual-E13-end\">Independent fair ±1 variables have mean 0, variance 1 and maximal span h=2, with a=−1. Sn is supported on −n+2Z. Disk areas follow exact binomial masses, with displayed numerator over 2^n; adjacent allowed cells have width 2. At k=n mod 2, the right rectangle has height φ(k/√n) and width h/√n in standardized coordinates. At finite n this is only a local approximation. Using h=1 halves it; forbidden-parity masses are exactly zero. The three n settings illustrate translation of the lattice, not a proof of the local CLT.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E13.en.svg\">Complete static SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E13.en.html\">Print view</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Independent fair ±1 variables have mean 0, variance 1 and maximal span h=2, with a=−1. Sn is supported on −n+2Z. Disk areas follow exact binomial masses, with displayed numerator over 2^n; adjacent allowed cells have width 2. At k=n mod 2, the right rectangle has height φ(k/√n) and width h/√n in standardized coordinates. At finite n this is only a local approximation. Using h=1 halves it; forbidden-parity masses are exactly zero. The three n settings illustrate translation of the lattice, not a proof of the local CLT.",
