      "id": "E17",
      "chapter": 17,
      "slug": "17-markov-chains",
      "section": "17.2",
      "title": "Compress the past, preserve the prediction",
      "lang": "en",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch2\" id=\"visual-E17\" data-batch2=\"E17\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E17</span><h3>Compress the past, preserve the prediction</h3></header><p class=\"\">00 and 10 end in the same bit, yet predict differently. 01 and 10 end differently, yet share the same posterior state.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-state=\"last\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Keep last bit</button><button type=\"button\" data-state=\"posterior\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Keep posterior q</button></div><div class=\"b2-single wide\"><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E17-en-last.svg\" alt=\"Four histories mapped into the selected information states\" data-state-scene></div><output data-reading>The same state 0 leads to two forecasts: information was lost.</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E17-end\">Choose Θ=1/4 or 3/4 with equal probability, then sample conditionally iid Bernoulli(Θ). For histories 00,10,01,11, q=P(Θ=3/4|history) equals 1/10,1/2,1/2,9/10; w(q)=1/4+q/2 gives predictions 3/10,1/2,1/2,7/10. Arrows are information maps, not equiprobable histories. The last bit cannot recover the original forecast; the posterior updates via the text’s T0,T1 and Markov kernel. No universal one-dimensional or unique minimal state is claimed, nor is future independence inferred from the picture.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E17.en.svg\">Complete static SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E17.en.html\">Print view</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Choose Θ=1/4 or 3/4 with equal probability, then sample conditionally iid Bernoulli(Θ). For histories 00,10,01,11, q=P(Θ=3/4|history) equals 1/10,1/2,1/2,9/10; w(q)=1/4+q/2 gives predictions 3/10,1/2,1/2,7/10. Arrows are information maps, not equiprobable histories. The last bit cannot recover the original forecast; the posterior updates via the text’s T0,T1 and Markov kernel. No universal one-dimensional or unique minimal state is claimed, nor is future independence inferred from the picture.",
