      "title": "同样在跳点取1，时间规则却不同",
      "lang": "zh",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch2\" id=\"visual-E30\" data-batch2=\"E30\" lang=\"zh\"><header><span>E30</span><h3>同样在跳点取1，时间规则却不同</h3></header><p class=\"\">到达时都取值1，不代表使用了同一份信息。全程事先选1，与看见跳跃才取1，时间测度读到的完全不同。</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">示意记录：0次</button><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">示意记录：2次</button><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"false\">示意记录：3次</button></div><div class=\"b2-pair\"><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>事前：全程取1</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30-zh-pre-2.svg\" alt=\"A predictable constant choice fills the whole time band\" data-pre-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >总体期望：0</p></section><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>事后：只选刚发生的跳点</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30-zh-after-2.svg\" alt=\"Jump-only choices are isolated instants of zero time length\" data-after-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >总体期望：3</p></section></div><output data-reading>这条记录的补偿收益：事前2−3=−1；事后2−0=2。</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E30-end\">率1 Poisson过程、通常增广自然滤过、K=3。左规则H≡1在(0,3]可预测，路径收益∫H dN−∫H dt=N₃−3，期望0。右规则Hₜ=ΔNₜ适应且可选，但不可预测；路径收益N₃−0，期望3。右图圆点是零长度时刻，不是窄的正长度区间；有限跳点对dt零测，对dN却各有质量1。三条手选记录只展示路径计算，未赋等概率、不是模拟、不能用来估计期望。总体期望来自E N₃=3，且自然滤过和无同时重跳的Poisson模型不可省略；未把此结论推广到任意滤过。</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30.zh.svg\">完整静态SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E30.zh.html\">打印页</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "率1 Poisson过程、通常增广自然滤过、K=3。左规则H≡1在(0,3]可预测，路径收益∫H dN−∫H dt=N₃−3，期望0。右规则Hₜ=ΔNₜ适应且可选，但不可预测；路径收益N₃−0，期望3。右图圆点是零长度时刻，不是窄的正长度区间；有限跳点对dt零测，对dN却各有质量1。三条手选记录只展示路径计算，未赋等概率、不是模拟、不能用来估计期望。总体期望来自E N₃=3，且自然滤过和无同时重跳的Poisson模型不可省略；未把此结论推广到任意滤过。",
      "status": "author visual review pending",
      "kind": "new explanation"
    },
    {
      "id": "E30",
      "chapter": 30,
      "slug": "30-predictability",
      "section": "30.1",
      "title": "Same value at arrivals, different time rules",
      "lang": "en",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch2\" id=\"visual-E30\" data-batch2=\"E30\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E30</span><h3>Same value at arrivals, different time rules</h3></header><p class=\"\">Both rules take value 1 at arrivals. But choosing 1 in advance and selecting only observed jump instants have different time costs.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Record: 0 arrivals</button><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Record: 2 arrivals</button><button type=\"button\" data-arrival-count=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Record: 3 arrivals</button></div><div class=\"b2-pair\"><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>Before: choose 1 throughout</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30-en-pre-2.svg\" alt=\"A predictable constant choice fills the whole time band\" data-pre-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >Population expectation: 0</p></section><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>After: select observed jump instants</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30-en-after-2.svg\" alt=\"Jump-only choices are isolated instants of zero time length\" data-after-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >Population expectation: 3</p></section></div><output data-reading>Compensated payoff on this record: before 2−3=−1; after 2−0=2.</output><figcaption id=\"visual-E30-end\">Rate-one Poisson process with its usual augmented natural filtration and K=3. The predictable choice H≡1 on (0,3] gives pathwise payoff N3−3, of expectation 0. Ht=ΔNt is adapted and optional but not predictable; it gives N3−0, of expectation 3. Dots denote zero-duration instants, not narrow positive-length intervals. Finitely many jumps have zero dt mass but unit dN mass each. The three hand-chosen records illustrate pathwise calculations only; they are not equiprobable or simulated estimates of expectations. Expectations use E N3=3. The natural filtration and simple Poisson jumps matter; no assertion for every filtration is made.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E30.en.svg\">Complete static SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E30.en.html\">Print view</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Rate-one Poisson process with its usual augmented natural filtration and K=3. The predictable choice H≡1 on (0,3] gives pathwise payoff N3−3, of expectation 0. Ht=ΔNt is adapted and optional but not predictable; it gives N3−0, of expectation 3. Dots denote zero-duration instants, not narrow positive-length intervals. Finitely many jumps have zero dt mass but unit dN mass each. The three hand-chosen records illustrate pathwise calculations only; they are not equiprobable or simulated estimates of expectations. Expectations use E N3=3. The natural filtration and simple Poisson jumps matter; no assertion for every filtration is made.",
      "status": "author visual review pending",
      "kind": "new explanation"
    },
    {
      "id": "E24",
      "chapter": 24,
      "slug": "24-path-convergence",
      "section": "24.13",
      "title": "对齐一次跳跃，不能删除一次往返",
      "lang": "zh",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch2\" id=\"visual-E24\" data-batch2=\"E24\" lang=\"zh\"><header><span>E24</span><h3>对齐一次跳跃，不能删除一次往返</h3></header><p class=\"\">两种变化都只发生在很短的时间里。左边只需移动发生时刻；右边却真的走到了高度1，再返回。</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-clock-key=\"4\" aria-pressed=\"true\">δ=1/4</button><button type=\"button\" data-clock-key=\"8\" aria-pressed=\"false\">δ=1/8</button><button type=\"button\" data-clock-key=\"16\" aria-pressed=\"false\">δ=1/16</button></div><div class=\"b2-pair\"><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>时间错位，可以对齐</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24-zh-4-jump-1.svg\" alt=\"Before and after a shifted step is aligned\" data-jump-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" data-jump-result>取值误差 0</p></section><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>短暂往返，不能删除</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24-zh-4-pulse-1.svg\" alt=\"Before and after a pulse still has height one\" data-pulse-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >取值误差 1</p></section></div><div class=\"e24-mobile\"><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24-zh-mobile-4-1.svg\" alt=\"Compact comparison with actual value errors\" data-compact-scene></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-clock-apply=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"true\">使用同一时钟</button><button type=\"button\" data-clock-apply=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">撤去时钟</button></div><details class=\"b2-tech\"><summary>第二层：时钟方向与J₁条件</summary><div class=\"b2-single\"><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24-zh-clock-4.svg\" alt=\"The increasing homeomorphism fixes 0 and 1 and maps a to a plus delta\" data-clock-scene></div><p class=\"\">上方参考时刻t → 下方原记录λ(t)。比较的是xδ∘λ与x；同一λ用于右侧往返与零函数的比较。</p></details><figcaption id=\"visual-E24-end\">a=1/2，0&lt;δ≤1/4。左x=1_[a,1]、xδ=1_[a+δ,1]；λ是经过(0,0),(a,a+δ),(1,1)的递增分段线性连续同胚。‖λ−id‖∞=δ，xδ∘λ=x。右zδ=1_[a+δ,a+δ+δ²)，参考是零函数；同一λ将其支撑变为[a,a+δ²(1−a)/(1−a−δ))。任何满射时间同胚都保留其上确界1，故不仅这幅图中的λ不能删除它。所有端点用实心/空心区别右连续取值；灰虚线是参考，实线是当前，不画竖直插值。δ→0时，左在J₁收敛，右不在J₁趋零。把发生时刻接近与振幅小分开，才是两场景的差别。</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24.zh.svg\">完整静态SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E24.zh.html\">打印页</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "a=1/2，0<δ≤1/4。左x=1_[a,1]、xδ=1_[a+δ,1]；λ是经过(0,0),(a,a+δ),(1,1)的递增分段线性连续同胚。‖λ−id‖∞=δ，xδ∘λ=x。右zδ=1_[a+δ,a+δ+δ²)，参考是零函数；同一λ将其支撑变为[a,a+δ²(1−a)/(1−a−δ))。任何满射时间同胚都保留其上确界1，故不仅这幅图中的λ不能删除它。所有端点用实心/空心区别右连续取值；灰虚线是参考，实线是当前，不画竖直插值。δ→0时，左在J₁收敛，右不在J₁趋零。把发生时刻接近与振幅小分开，才是两场景的差别。",
      "status": "author visual review pending",
      "kind": "structural revision"
    },
    {
      "id": "E24",
      "chapter": 24,
      "slug": "24-path-convergence",
      "section": "24.13",
      "title": "Align a jump; never erase a pulse",
      "lang": "en",
      "html": "<figure class=\"batch2\" id=\"visual-E24\" data-batch2=\"E24\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>E24</span><h3>Align a jump; never erase a pulse</h3></header><p class=\"\">Both changes occupy little time. The left only shifts when a jump occurs. The right actually visits height 1 and returns.</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-clock-key=\"4\" aria-pressed=\"true\">δ=1/4</button><button type=\"button\" data-clock-key=\"8\" aria-pressed=\"false\">δ=1/8</button><button type=\"button\" data-clock-key=\"16\" aria-pressed=\"false\">δ=1/16</button></div><div class=\"b2-pair\"><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>A time shift can be aligned</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24-en-4-jump-1.svg\" alt=\"Before and after a shifted step is aligned\" data-jump-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" data-jump-result>Value error 0</p></section><section class=\"b2-panel\"><h4>A brief pulse cannot be erased</h4><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24-en-4-pulse-1.svg\" alt=\"Before and after a pulse still has height one\" data-pulse-scene><p class=\"b2-result\" >Value error 1</p></section></div><div class=\"e24-mobile\"><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24-en-mobile-4-1.svg\" alt=\"Compact comparison with actual value errors\" data-compact-scene></div><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-clock-apply=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Apply the same clock</button><button type=\"button\" data-clock-apply=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Remove clock</button></div><details class=\"b2-tech\"><summary>Technical layer: clock direction and J₁</summary><div class=\"b2-single\"><img class=\"ex-svg\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24-en-clock-4.svg\" alt=\"The increasing homeomorphism fixes 0 and 1 and maps a to a plus delta\" data-clock-scene></div><p class=\"\">Reference time t (top) → original time λ(t) (bottom). Compare xδ∘λ with x; use the same λ to compare the pulse with zero.</p></details><figcaption id=\"visual-E24-end\">Let a=1/2, 0&lt;δ≤1/4. Left: x=1_[a,1], xδ=1_[a+δ,1]. The piecewise-linear increasing continuous homeomorphism λ passes through (0,0),(a,a+δ),(1,1). Thus ‖λ−id‖∞=δ and xδ∘λ=x. Right: zδ=1_[a+δ,a+δ+δ²), compared with zero. The same λ moves its support to [a,a+δ²(1−a)/(1−a−δ)). Every onto time homeomorphism preserves supremum 1; the impossibility is not inferred from one chosen clock. Filled/open endpoints specify right-continuous values; gray dashes are the reference, solid lines the record; no vertical interpolation is drawn. As δ→0 the left converges in J1, while the right cannot tend to zero in J1. Small timing error and small amplitude error are different requirements.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-early-v2/E24.en.svg\">Complete static SVG</a><a href=\"/print/E24.en.html\">Print view</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Let a=1/2, 0<δ≤1/4. Left: x=1_[a,1], xδ=1_[a+δ,1]. The piecewise-linear increasing continuous homeomorphism λ passes through (0,0),(a,a+δ),(1,1). Thus ‖λ−id‖∞=δ and xδ∘λ=x. Right: zδ=1_[a+δ,a+δ+δ²), compared with zero. The same λ moves its support to [a,a+δ²(1−a)/(1−a−δ)). Every onto time homeomorphism preserves supremum 1; the impossibility is not inferred from one chosen clock. Filled/open endpoints specify right-continuous values; gray dashes are the reference, solid lines the record; no vertical interpolation is drawn. As δ→0 the left converges in J1, while the right cannot tend to zero in J1. Small timing error and small amplitude error are different requirements.",
